      "findings": [
        {
          "finding": "GITHUB_EVENT_NAME survives cleanEnvironment, so in a CI pull request job jest runs the existing skill-record fixtures in pull request mode. With the fixture helper inheriting process.env, 10 of 12 tests failed (pr5d/ci-env-without-isolation.log). The helper now unsets it.",
          "cites": "Steps 3",
          "commit": "053ae2b",
          "patch": "2ec6ecc48bad2ea246c3206d3228d5e2d627e987"
        },
        {
          "finding": "The fact the change depends on: hosted CI runs verify:current without --base, so the skill-records range check never runs there, and the new rule has no effect in CI until the workflow fetches history and passes --base.",
          "cites": "Steps 2",
          "none": "Workflow edits are out of scope for 5d. docs/skills.md Limits says so, and work/skill-process-evidence/ci-range-checks.patch is the pending activation."
        },
        {
          "finding": "A rebase merge rewrites every SHA. A replay of the stack onto e22c06d shared no SHA with the branch, and skills:check e22c06d HEAD still passed outside pull request mode, through patch-ids and the base binding.",
          "cites": "Steps 5",
          "none": "Proved in pr5d/rebase-merge-simulation-8ac891b.log. No change needed."
        }
      ],
